{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided. The rules for solving the Sudoku puzzle are similar to the standard rules, with a unique twist. The numbers in the cells that are enclosed by grey lines must add up to the numbers shown in the corner. This twist adds a new layer of complexity to the puzzle, requiring careful consideration of the numbers and their relationships to each other.\n\n\n \nAddition to the standard Sudoku rules, the numbers within each shape formed by grey lines cannot be repeated. This means that each shape must contain a unique set of numbers, which can make the puzzle more challenging to solve. The puzzle is a fun and engaging way to challenge one's problem-solving skills and logical thinking.\n\n\n \nThe completed puzzle can be found in next week's Observer Digital Edition. This provides a convenient way for readers to check their answers and see the solution to the puzzle. The Observer Digital Edition is a valuable resource for readers who enjoy puzzles and games, and want to stay up-to-date with the latest news and information.\n\n\n \nThe Sudoku puzzle is a popular and entertaining activity that can be enjoyed by people of all ages. The unique rules and twist on the standard game make it a fun and challenging way to exercise one's brain and improve problem-solving skills. The puzzle is a great way to relax and unwind, while also providing a sense of accomplishment and satisfaction when solved.\n\n\n \nThe print version of the article can be accessed by clicking on the provided link. The Sudoku puzzle is a great way to challenge oneself and have fun at the same time. With its unique rules and twist on the standard game, it is an activity that can be enjoyed by people of all ages and skill levels, and is a great way to stay